      "writtenOn": "2022-08-05T12:57:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Sir:\n\n1.we will only protect the last lock.\nif:lock(a); lock(b); unlock(a); unlock(b).\nresult:we only protect lock(b), and starttime will be clear in unlock(a).\n\nBecause we just want to protect the locking-process for a short time, and we found\nthat the method which protects the last lock can solve more than 70% issues in our\nproject. \n\n2. Most of the rest issue is as follows:\n\nprocess1: lock(b)  -\u003e ............................  -\u003e unlock(b)\nprocess2: lock(a)  -\u003e lock(b)  -\u003e lock(b)_contended -\u003e runnable \nprocess3:                                              lock(a)  -\u003e lock(a)_contended \n\n- process3 is a important process, but it block in lock(a).\n- lock(a) is held by process2, but process2 is runnable, although lock(b) is released by process1.\n\nthe above issue we had solved without any hooks in our .ko.",
      "parentUuid": "b90626eb_f8b9f211",
      "revId": "6e6621735a644b75bcbc41878073d6301a1ce56b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
